{
  "number": 3388,
  "title": "OpenAIModel (Responses, TypeScript) sends invalid assistant history shape, rejected by Bedrock Mantle",
  "url": "https://github.com/strands-agents/harness-sdk/issues/3388",
  "state": "closed",
  "created_at": "2026-07-21T15:51:53Z",
  "closed_at": "2026-07-21T19:47:13Z",
  "body": "### SDK Language\n\nTypeScript\n\n### Steps to Reproduce\n\nThe OpenAI Responses adapter serializes assistant history into an invalid `input` item shape when replaying multi-turn conversations without server-side state (`stateful: false`).\n\nFor a two-turn conversation, `formatResponsesMessages` in `strands-ts/src/models/openai/responses-adapter.ts` emits the assistant turn as:\n\n```json\n{ \"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": [{ \"type\": \"output_text\", \"text\": \"...\" }] }\n```\n\nThis matches neither valid OpenAI `input` shape for an assistant turn:\n- `EasyInputMessage` (string content): `{ \"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": \"...\" }`\n- `ResponseOutputMessage` (full item): requires `type: \"message\"`, `id`, `status`, and `output_text` with `annotations`.\n\nThe emitted object is a bare `{ role, content: [output_text] }` missing all the `ResponseOutputMessage` required fields, so it is not a valid input item. The code cast it away with `as unknown as ResponseInputItem`, and its own comment acknowledged the shape was incomplete.\n\nReproduce with the Bedrock Mantle integ test `test/integ/models/openai/mantle.test.node.ts > handles reasoning content across multi-turn conversations` (requires live Bedrock Mantle credentials).\n\n### Expected Behavior\n\nText-only assistant history is serialized as a valid, OpenAI-documented shape and accepted by both OpenAI-hosted and Bedrock Mantle.\n\n### Actual Behavior\n\nBedrock Mantle's strict Responses schema rejects the request:\n\n```\nSubmitRequestFailure: code=-32602, msg=220 validation errors for ResponsesRequest\n```\n\nOpenAI-hosted tolerates the malformed shape (fills in / ignores the missing fields), so the bug was invisible there. It only surfaced once PR #3290 made terminal `response.failed` stream events throw instead of finalizing as an empty successful response, which turned the previously-swallowed Mantle rejection into a loud failure.\n\n### Possible Solution\n\nN/A\n\n### Related Issues\n\nThe Python SDK has the identical bug at `strands-py/src/strands/models/openai_responses.py` (`_format_request_message_content` emits `output_text` for assistant text); fix both for parity.\n\nSurfaced by #3290.\n",
